content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "Four parts and the tests defined before the first principle; each principle carries name/statement/rationale/implications only; all principle cross-references (screen columns, history) use slugs, never numbers"}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "Every statement is decidable yes/no alone; obligations are one per bullet with conditionals kept inside their bullet; decision terms are defined in-statement (e.g. use-defined-terms' importance criterion) or covered by the opening's glossary pointer"}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "All nine rationales show a generic failure, none references product operational history; citations (Deming, ASD-STE100/ISO 704, least privilege) are well-known external sources"}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Implications are one per bullet, each traceable to a statement clause with a named actor (authors, reviewers, maintainers, whoever opens/closes/runs); two actors are grammatically implicit but recoverable — stumble, not fail"}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "Nine columns match nine principles, all five opening tests have rows, and every claimed pass is reproducible; the two extra (mechanical)/(judged) rows sit under a heading that says 'the intro's tests' — a labeling stumble only"}
  - {scenario: 6, result: pass, notes: "Each principle rejects concrete work (self-checked work, ambient notes, orphan activities, coined terms, bespoke forms, copies, consumer-less channels, artifact-only done, ambient loads) and the opposite is a rule real honest shops run"}
  - {scenario: mechanical, result: pass, notes: "MUST/MUST NOT appear only in statements; capitals elsewhere are only the opening's BCP 14 mentions; standalone 'NOT' in the Lencioni row is not a BCP 14 keyword"}
stumbles: ["A check that cannot cite the definition clause it projects has no standing", "(Deming: cease dependence on inspection; build quality in — and still inspect.)", "a hand edit to a rendering is reverted, not merged", "Fitness screen (the intro's tests; sources: TOGAF, Spool, Rumelt, Lencioni)"]
top_changes: ["Replace the verb 'projects' in define-good-up-front's second implication with a plain or glossary-defined verb such as 'checks'", "Give the Deming citation a named work, matching the fully-cited opening sources", "Name the actor in single-source-of-truth's rendering implication (who reverts the hand edit)", "Retitle the fitness-screen heading or fold the (mechanical) and (judged) rows into the opening's stated tests so the heading's claim matches the rows"]
